Spec: Metrics

Purpose:
  Instrument every Vynil reconcile with Prometheus data: four prefix-kept registries, one per
    custom resource kind, each holding a reconcile-attempts counter, a failure counter
    labelled by the @Error::metric_label text, and a duration histogram whose observations
    carry an optional `trace_id` exemplar. Hand the registries out as @Arc fields so
    @Manager::metrics (./manager.rs) can render them, and time a reconcile through the RAII
    @ReconcileMeasurerBox and @ReconcileMeasurerInstance measurers, which observe the duration
    exactly once when they drop.

Owns:
  ./metrics.rs

References:
  ./telemetry.sdd — @get_trace_id supplies every @count_and_measure trace id today; its stub
    returns @TraceId::INVALID, which keeps the exemplar lane this file offers dead.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — the @Error vocabulary and @Error::metric_label whose lowercased
    @Debug text becomes the `error` label; that spec's open `[?]` on unbounded labels applies
    here directly.
  /common/src/jukebox.sdd, /common/src/instancesystem.sdd, /common/src/instanceservice.sdd,
    /common/src/instancetenant.sdd — the four namespaced CR models whose metadata and spec
    fields are read verbatim into label values.
  ./manager.sdd, ./main.rs — specs pending; their owners read the four @Registry fields and
    serve `/metrics`; this file serves nothing.

Depends on:
  @prometheus_client `0.24.0` (../Cargo.toml, locked `0.24.1`) — @Registry and @Unit,
    @Counter, @Family, @HistogramWithExemplars, the @EncodeLabelSet derive, and the OpenMetrics
    text encoder the @Arc registries eventually feed.
  @kube (locked kube-core `3.1.0`, /Cargo.lock) — @kube::@ResourceExt with @name_any and
    @namespace producing the identity label values.
  @common — @Error and the CR types @JukeBox, @SystemInstance, @ServiceInstance and
    @TenantInstance.
  @opentelemetry `0.32.0` — @TraceId and @TraceId::INVALID crossing in from ./telemetry.rs.
  `tokio` time — @tokio::time::@Instant, the monotonic std alias; @elapsed is the sole clock.

Must:
  Stay crate-internal by module: ./lib.rs declares `mod metrics;` and re-exports only
    @Metrics; every other type here is `pub` inside the private @crate::metrics path —
    ./instance_common.rs and the three kind modules name @ReconcileMeasurerInstance in their
    @InstanceKind surface, and the bin crate (a separate crate over lib `controller`) reaches
    these metrics only as the @String returned by @Manager::metrics.
  Build exactly four registries in @Metrics::default, prefix-only via
    @Registry::with_prefix with the literal prefixes `jukebox_reconcile`,
    `system_instance_reconcile`, `service_instance_reconcile` and
    `tenant_instance_reconcile`, then wrap each in @Arc as @reg_box, @reg_sys, @reg_svc and
    @reg_tnt; no const registry labels are set.
  Register three families per kind before publishing — @register calls @register_with_unit
    (`"duration"`, help `"reconcile duration"`, @Unit::Seconds), @register (`"failures"`, help
    `"reconciliation errors"`) and @register (`"runs"`, help `"reconciliations"`) in that
    order, cloning each @Family handle into the registry, then returns the metric set unchanged.
  Render through @prometheus_client `0.24.1` text encoding as prefix-joined names: the
    `<prefix>_runs_total` and `<prefix>_failures_total` counters, and the
    `<prefix>_duration_seconds` histogram (`# TYPE … histogram`, a `# UNIT … seconds` line,
    `_bucket`, `_sum` and `_count` series); that encoder version emits no `# created` lines;
    twelve families total across the four registries.
  Set every duration histogram to the same nine sorted bounds
    `[0.01, 0.1, 0.5, 1., 5., 15., 60., 120., 300.]` seconds in each kind's @Default via
    @Family::new_with_constructor, so a
    child histogram is born only when a new label set is first observed.
  Measure duration identically in both measurer @Drop impls: elapsed integer millis from
    `self.start.elapsed().as_millis()` cast with `as f64 / 1000.0` — integer truncation, so
    sub-millisecond runs observe `0.0` — carried under
    `#[allow(clippy::cast_precision_loss)]`, then
    `.get_or_create(&self.labels).observe(duration, trace, None)` with the exemplar timestamp
    pinned at @None; the @Clone of
    @Family inside @count_and_measure is what lets @Drop write back into the registered
    histogram.
  Treat @Drop as the single writer of duration observations: normal end of scope, an early `?`
    return and a panic unwind all drop the measurer and still record exactly one observation
    whose value is the time since @count_and_measure was called.
  Count a run, not a completion: @count_and_measure increments the runs counter immediately at
    call inside the reconciles (./jukebox.rs @reconcile binds the measurer as `let _mes = …`,
    ./instance_common.rs @run_with_finalizer binds it through @count_and_measure_metrics), so
    an attempt that fails still counts; no success counter exists anywhere, making success
    inferable only as runs minus failures.
  Attach exemplars with exactly one label (@trace_id) — @count_and_measure converts the borrowed
    @TraceId through the @TryFrom<&@TraceId> impl via `.ok()`; the impl compares with
    @std::matches! and returns @Err(@Error::Other("Invalid trace ID")) for @TraceId::INVALID,
    else @Ok carrying `id.to_string()`, which opentelemetry `0.32` renders as exactly 32
    lowercase hex digits; the discarded @Err means a refused id silently yields no exemplar
    while the observation itself is kept.
  Label failures with the error text: @reconcile_failure performs one `.inc()` on the kind's
    failures family with `error` set to @Error::metric_label of the caller's @Error, plus
    `instance` (jukebox) or `name` and the spec strings (instances) per Exposes.
  Label identity the kube-core `3.1.0` way: @name_any resolves the metadata @name, then
    @generate_name, else the empty string — `3.1` never joins the namespace — and @namespace
    is @Option of metadata.namespace, so nameless objects land on `""` values;
    @prometheus_client encodes an @Option<@String> label as empty when @None; the instance
    labels clone @spec.jukebox, @category and @package verbatim.
  Grow series monotonically: @Family::get_or_create creates and stores a child permanently on
    any unseen label set across runs, failures and duration; nothing here ever deletes,
    rebases or caps a child, so series are unbounded by construction.
  Serve all four kind registries from live call sites: the tenant @Default and @register run
    inside @Metrics::default identically and ./instancetenant.rs invokes the tenant
    @count_and_measure and @reconcile_failure exactly as ./instanceservice.rs and
    ./instancesystem.rs do, so no shipped family encodes as metadata-only; the jukebox family
    is driven by ./jukebox.rs @count_and_measure on its own reconcile entry.
  Stay independent per @Metrics::default call: separate registries and counters, built once
    per @Manager by ./manager.rs and fresh in ./jukebox.rs @make_test_ctx; satisfy the ./lib.rs
    `deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used)` with zero unwrap or expect sites — the
    file's only failure is laundered through `.ok()`.

Must not:
  Serve or encode: no endpoint, port, HTTP type or @encode_registry call lives here — even
    the OpenMetrics `# EOF` termination of the `/metrics` body belongs to @Manager::metrics
    and ./main.rs.

Exposes:
  @Metrics — `pub` struct deriving @Clone and @Debug with pub fields @jukebox
    (@ReconcileMetricsJukebox), @system_instance, @service_instance, @tenant_instance, and the
    export handles @reg_box, @reg_sys, @reg_svc and @reg_tnt, each @Arc<@Registry>; re-exported
    at the controller crate root as the module's only externally nameable item; @Clone copies
    live handles into the same registries.
  @Default for @Metrics — constructs and registers all four kinds into their four prefixed
    registries as Must pins.
  @LabelBox — @EncodeLabelSet with one Rust field @name rendering label `name`, the jukebox
    identity; derives @Clone, @Hash, @Eq, @Debug, @Default.
  @LabelInstance — @EncodeLabelSet with fields @name, @namespace (@Option<@String>), @jukebox,
    @category and @package rendering labels `name`, `namespace`, `jukebox`, `category`,
    `package`; same derives; one type shared by all three instance kinds' runs and duration
    families, so an instance whose `category` or `package` changes moves to fresh series.
  @TraceLabel — @EncodeLabelSet with field @trace_id rendering `trace_id`; derives @Default
    (empty string) but no call site uses it; implements @TryFrom<&@TraceId> with @Error = @Error
    per the exemplar rule in Must.
  @ErrorLabels — @EncodeLabelSet fields @instance and @error rendering `instance`, `error`;
    derives @Clone, @Hash, @Eq and @Debug only, no @Default; the jukebox failures family.
  @ErrorLabelsInstance — @EncodeLabelSet fields @name, @namespace, @jukebox, @category,
    @package and @error rendering six labels — @LabelInstance's five plus `error`; no
    @Default; the three instance failures families.
  @ReconcileMeasurerBox and @ReconcileMeasurerInstance — `pub` structs deriving @Debug with
    four private fields (@start of type @tokio::time::@Instant, private @labels, private @trace
    as @Option<@TraceLabel>, private @metric family handle); unconstructable outside this file
    and observation-free until @Drop; both @Drop impls are identical code over their label and
    family types, so @ReconcileMeasurerInstance serves all three instance kinds.
  The four same-shaped family sets — @ReconcileMetricsJukebox, @ReconcileMetricsSystemInstance,
    @ReconcileMetricsTenantInstance and @ReconcileMetricsServiceInstance, `pub` structs with
    pub fields @runs, @failures and @duration typed @Family<@LabelBox, @Counter>,
    @Family<@ErrorLabels, @Counter> and @Family<@LabelBox, @HistogramWithExemplars<@TraceLabel>>
    for the jukebox, with @LabelInstance and @ErrorLabelsInstance swapped in for the three
    instance kinds.
  `pub fn @register(self, r: &mut @Registry) -> Self` per set — the registration sequence in
    Must; consumes and returns the same handles.
  `pub fn @reconcile_failure(&self, doc, e: &@Error)` per set, doc typed @JukeBox,
    @SystemInstance, @TenantInstance or @ServiceInstance respectively — one failures @inc()
    with the label set Must describes.
  `pub fn @count_and_measure(&self, doc, trace_id: &@TraceId) -> measurer` per set — one runs
    @inc() on the kind's label set plus the started measurer.

Accepts:
  A registered @JukeBox, @SystemInstance, @ServiceInstance or @TenantInstance reference at
    each @reconcile_failure or @count_and_measure call; @count_and_measure additionally needs a
    borrowed @TraceId and nothing is retained beyond the family handles; @register borrows the
    target @Registry mutably for the call only.
  This module validates nothing: absent name, @generate_name or namespace become empty label
    values, and any spec text — however free-form — becomes a label verbatim; the CR references
    need not stay alive after the call. No config, env var or CRD field feeds this file
    otherwise.

Returns:
  @Metrics::default — a fully registered struct; every family child is still lazy, so an
    untouched instance encodes as twelve HELP/TYPE stanzas, four `# UNIT … seconds` lines and
    no samples, and @Clone hands those same live families to a second owner.
  @count_and_measure — the runs increment is the side effect; the measurer has no public
    accessor, so its only observable return is the one @Drop-time observation.
  @register returns @Self carrying exactly the registered family handles; @reconcile_failure
    returns @() after exactly one increment.
  @TryFrom<&@TraceId> for @TraceLabel — @Ok carrying the 32-lowercase-hex id, or @Err per
    Raises; @count_and_measure keeps only @Ok, as an @Option exemplar.

Raises:
  @Err(@Error::Other("Invalid trace ID")) from the sole fallible item, the
    @TryFrom<&@TraceId> impl for @TraceLabel, on a @TraceId::INVALID receiver; @count_and_measure
    discards it via `.ok()` — the refusal, its text and its missing project stable-id are never
    visible anywhere (see Tasks).
  Nothing else in the file is fallible: @Default, @register, @reconcile_failure,
    @count_and_measure and both @Drop impls cannot return or propagate any error, and the fixed
    sorted bucket list forecloses the prometheus-client bucket-layout panic; no input produces a
    panic.

Handles:
  @TraceId::INVALID — the @get_trace_id stub's only output — refused to @None exemplar, so
    today every observation across all four kinds lands exemplar-free; the @Ok arm exists but
    no real id ever reaches it in shipped builds.
  New label combinations on any family — a fresh @Family child is created and kept; repeats
    reuse the existing child; any two instances whose five instance labels collide share one
    child.
  A reconcile that returns early or panics — the in-scope measurer drops mid-way and its
    shorter duration is still observed against the already-counted run.
  Absent metadata — `name` and `instance` empty through the @None fallback chain of @name_any,
    `namespace` empty through the @Option label encoding.
  Tenant traffic — children appear through the ./instancetenant.rs @count_and_measure and
    @reconcile_failure call sites exactly like the other kinds.

Tasks:
  [ ] Map coverage from the Scenarios below: @Metrics::default inventory (names, help strings,
      units, bucket bounds, metadata-only encoding) through a throwaway registry; the immediate
      runs increment in @count_and_measure; the @Drop observation with `0.0` truncation under
      1 ms; both @TryFrom arms; @reconcile_failure label content and same-error series reuse;
      and cross-kind independence. No test anywhere in the workspace asserts a
      metric value today — ./jukebox.rs @make_test_ctx builds a @Metrics but never reads it
      back.
  [?] The failures `error` label is @Error::metric_label — full lowercased @Debug with payload
      text (paths, URLs, job names) — so failures series are unbounded by error detail, the
      decision already `[?]` in /common/src/lib.sdd. Decide here too whether to shorten the
      label to the variant name.
  [?] The free-text `category`, `package` and `jukebox` labels plus `name` and `namespace` make
      runs and duration cardinality grow with every CR and every spec edit, permanently, and
      nothing prunes series after an instance is deleted. Decide later whether that churn is
      acceptable for a low-scale selfhosted controller.
  [?] `runs` counts attempts at entry, not outcomes, and no success counter exists, so the
      parent ./operator.sdd Must promising "success/failure counters" is unsatisfiable by this
      inventory — success stays inferred. Decide the success semantics, then the metric set.
  [?] The parent's "last-event timestamp" metric is implemented nowhere in this file, nor as a
      gauge anywhere. Decide later whether to add it or drop the parent wording.
  [?] With @get_trace_id hardcoded to @TraceId::INVALID (the ./telemetry.sdd `[?]`), every
      exemplar, the @TryFrom @Ok arm and the whole `trace_id` label are dead on production
      paths. Resolve jointly with that stub decision.
  [?] @Error::Other("Invalid trace ID") carries no stable unique id (project rule) and is
      silently laundered by `.ok()`, never logged or counted. Decide later whether refused ids
      deserve a visible counter.
  [?] On a kube upgrade the label values shift silently: the cached kube-core `4.0.0` makes
      @name_any return `"namespace name"` for the four namespaced CRs, renaming every existing
      `name` and `instance` series. Decide later whether to pre-join the namespace and pin
      kube.
  [?] @Metrics derives @Clone, duplicating live handles into the same registries, while
      ./manager.rs stores it as @Arc<@Metrics> and nothing clones today. Decide whether the
      @Clone derive stays.

Done when:
  Every Scenario has a green mapped test or a decided `[?]` Task, the cardinality and success
    decisions are recorded, and `cargo test -p operator` with clippy, fmt and `specdd lint` are
    green.

Scenario: Fresh metrics expose metadata only
  Given a @Metrics::default with no reconcile ever run
  When its four registries are text-encoded
  Then each registry carries exactly its prefixed runs and failures counters plus the
    `<prefix>_duration_seconds` histogram in the Must shape — twelve HELP/TYPE stanzas and
    four UNIT lines, with `0.24.1` adding no `# created` lines — and not one sample line
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: A JukeBox reconcile counts then measures
  Given ./jukebox.rs @reconcile binding @count_and_measure for a JukeBox whose metadata name
    is `vynil-box`
  When @count_and_measure runs
  Then the child for `name="vynil-box"` of `jukebox_reconcile_runs_total` incs immediately,
    before any reconcile work
  And when the reconcile ends and the measurer drops, one observation equal to integer
    milliseconds divided by `1000` — truncated, so a 400 microsecond reconcile observes `0.0` —
    lands on `jukebox_reconcile_duration_seconds` under the same labels
  And the same @Drop path serves the three instance kinds through @ReconcileMeasurerInstance
    with the five-label @LabelInstance set
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Invalid or absent trace drops the exemplar only
  Given @get_trace_id handing @count_and_measure @TraceId::INVALID — the value every shipped
    call sees today
  When the measurer drops
  Then the observation is recorded normally but with no exemplar, because @TryFrom refused
    with @Error::Other("Invalid trace ID") and `.ok()` discarded it
  But with any valid 32-digit id the observation would attach a `# EXEMPLAR` on its bucket
    line labelled `trace_id` — the lane no shipped build reaches
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Failures label by the full error text
  Given a reconcile failing with @Error::Other("boom") for jukebox `vynil-box` through the
    failure path calling @reconcile_failure
  When the increment lands
  Then exactly one growth on the child with `instance="vynil-box"` and `error` literally
    `other("boom")` — the @Error::metric_label lowercased @Debug
  And a failure whose @Debug payload differs (second message, path or job name) opens a
    brand-new permanent series while byte-identical text reuses the existing child
  And for the instance kinds the same increment goes to `<prefix>_failures_total` under the
    six @ErrorLabelsInstance labels
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: Instance kinds never share samples
  Given the three instance @Family sets are separate objects — shared by @Clone of the label
    types only — living in distinct registries
  When a @SystemInstance and a @ServiceInstance reconcile with all five label values identical
  Then each kind's own `<prefix>_runs_total` child grows independently and the shared
    @LabelInstance, @ErrorLabelsInstance and @ReconcileMeasurerInstance types cross no boundary
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: All kind registries expose children after reconciles
  Given jukes, systems, services and tenants each reconciled at least once in a shipped build
    (the tenant leg runs through ./instancetenant.rs @reconcile/@error_policy)
  When the exposition is scraped
  Then all four `<prefix>_runs_total` families carry at least one child and no shipped family
    is metadata-only
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  exposition head of one counted-kind histogram:
    `# HELP jukebox_reconcile_duration_seconds reconcile duration`
    `# TYPE jukebox_reconcile_duration_seconds histogram`
    `# UNIT jukebox_reconcile_duration_seconds seconds`
  hypothetical failures child today: child of `instance="vynil-box"` where `error` holds
    `other("boom")`
  valid-trace exemplar value shape: `trace_id` holding `80e1af3fb7e645135287ed5b6e99f252`
